    "description": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Provence covers the southeast of France, from the Rhône valley east toward the Alps and south to the Mediterranean. Its landscapes change quickly: limestone ridges, vineyards, olive groves and plateaus of lavender.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Villages such as Gordes and Roussillon sit on hilltops in the Luberon, built from pale stone or ochre-coloured walls. The Cistercian abbey at Sénanque stands in a valley close to Gordes. Aix-en-Provence adds shaded avenues, fountains and daily markets.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Late June and July bring the lavender bloom and the largest crowds. May, early June and September are quieter and still warm. Book rooms early for July.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
